@copy plain.qld
@rows 50
# M1 again on 80 by 50 (`@rows 50` is the /50 switch on DOS): the same keys, so the saved file matches the 25-row run byte for byte.
# The same tokens go to DOSBox's AUTOTYPE and to the host's script player.
f10 down enter                  # File > Open...
p l a i n period q l d enter    # the file name
h e l l o space enter           # typed at the start of the centred title, then Enter splits it
down down z bspace           # onto the next paragraph, a letter and back out
f10 down down enter             # File > Save
f10 down down down down down down down enter   # File > Exit
